## Mission
- Version: 1.0
- ID: P16-M3-M5-SHUTDOWN-RECOVERY-R5-PROTOCOL
- Title: Prospective shutdown-recovery protocol only
- Objective: Draft, review and archive a new prospective R5 recovery mission based on exact commit 5ed9a6854248cd250a097a9e657519ad0a057f64. No scientific execution.

## Context
R4 stopped after owner-reported shutdown. Its 3040 complete passes, one incomplete attempt and 2478 unattempted tasks are preserved. Existing published metadata only may inform this protocol.


## Requirements
- Verify exact BASE and clean branch preflight.
- Preserve all historical source, evidence, reviews and scientific STOP verdicts.
- Deliver a separately named prospective R5 mission protocol; current scope is drafting only.
- Bind original scientific, numerical, source, cohort and task definitions by exact hashes.
- Enumerate 952 R3 plus 3040 R4 optimizer reuse targets without admitting them now.
- Enumerate 216 analytic B0 reuse targets with no optimizer ftol label.
- Require a new independent saved-only eligibility audit of every optimizer and B0 state before future fitting.
- Specify source, A, features, masks, scalers, packing, initialization, objective, ridge, bounds, seed, certificates, runtime and journal checks per state.
- Retain R3 ftol1e-12 and R4 ftol0 provenance; prohibit counterfactual execution-equivalence claims.
- Exclude original failed R3, feasibility-diagnostic endpoint and incomplete R4 endpoint from reuse.
- Fix exactly 2479 remaining ordered task identities from the published R4 outcomes.
- Distinguish 2478 unattempted tasks from the single interrupted task.
- Start every future new task from its original frozen initializer; prohibit partial/failed/feasibility warm starts.
- Set a distinct prospective preflight/audit budget and new real-A stage budget; do not reset the old stage.
- Bound new attempts, optimizer FG calls, accepted iterations, derivative certificates and concurrency.
- Define inclusive per-attempt limits, pre-call denial and wall/boot/interruption semantics.
- Prohibit retries, replacement seeds/solvers, deadline resets and budget increases after failure.
- Preserve mathematical models, features, penalties, grid, seeds, scaling, masks, units, bounds and scientific thresholds.
- Preserve ftol0 policy, PG<=1e-5, AD<=1e-8, frozen FD h1e-5/error<=2e-5 and original checkpoints.
- Preserve all three D/S seeds and original A-only objective/tie selection.
- Preserve historical lambda1 B1-only B selection; forbid B reselection or E-driven tuning.
- Use only existing verified Development A saved inputs; missing mandatory state causes STOP, not source reacquisition.
- Preserve all 27 admitted Development and 27 locked Final identities and source boundaries.
- Prospectively register required future synthetic, numerical, role and process-guard tests without running them now.
- Require independent pre-execution acceptance of complete reuse audit and exact future implementation freeze.
- Require every original mandatory task and complete per-state provenance in full M4, without overwriting originals.
- Require independent complete-M4 acceptance before even considering an E release.
- Do not authorize E now; require separate explicit E authority plus complete M4 and one-batch controls.
- Preserve all original E models, six contrasts, sensitivities, controls and statistical requirements if later authorized.
- Forbid Final C/D, M6, P17, new dataset searches and unrelated custody engineering.
- Specify exact STOP triggers and preservation of partial, failed and unattempted tasks.
- Disclose post-A/B methodological exposure, historical state reuse and exploratory interpretation.
- Do not interpret engineering/protocol acceptance as numerical admission, M4 completion or scientific PASS.
- Freeze atomic current drafting requirements and verify all individually.
- Run only metadata, hash, task-set and document consistency checks in this delivery.
- Obtain an independent protocol review and preserve unsuccessful findings.
- Commit only the new protocol namespace and evidence; preserve the pinned daily-operations history.
- Provide exact normal origin/test handoff, file-hash readback and clean gate for protocol files only.
- Record zero new fits, objective/gradient/AD/FD calls, neural source requests and E/Final access.
- Stop after protocol delivery; require separate execution authorization tied to final protocol commit.


